<p style=3D"line-height:125%">I took the C train from Brooklyn to observe. =
What drives the people behind the spectacle? As one California-based dog ha=
ndler told me, =E2=80=9CNumber one, you have to be competitive. And you hav=
e to love the dogs.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">You also have to be willing to sink a small f=
ortune into breeding, grooming, training, feeding, and showing your prospec=
tive prize-winners, with no guarantee of a return on investment.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%"><strong>An expansive economic ecosystem</stro=
ng></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Dogs like Abigail don=E2=80=99t just come out=
 for the big show.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Owners vying for a national title will typica=
lly run a =E2=80=9Ccampaign=E2=80=9D to raise a dog=E2=80=99s national rank=
ing in the year leading up to the top contest. That may involve competing i=
n dozens or <a href=3D"https://d2q-Vf04.na1.hubspotlinks.com/Ctc/UB+113/d2q=
-Vf04/VWSg6n2lt59WW8lTDvM4C1FzMVLsY3L5KgzHXN8XrLD-4ZD0CW5BWr2F6lZ3ldW5lLMM8=
